# dependencies
node_modules/

# build output. The source of truth is src/ plus manifest.json; the bundle is generated.
dist/
build/
# A release build writes these two at the repository root, which is where the release workflow
# uploads them from and where the attestation reads them. Anchored on purpose: an unanchored
# styles.css would also hide src/styles.css, which is the real source of the plugin's styles.
/main.js
/styles.css
main.js.map
*.build.map

# build.js deploys into the dev vault, but Obsidian also drops state here whenever this
# project is opened as a vault itself - none of it is source.
.obsidian/
workspace.json
workspace-mobile.json
data.json

# Local tooling that happens to sit beside the plugin's source: griddle's session state at the
# repo root, and the .agents skills folder. Neither is part of the plugin, and both stay on the
# disk of whoever runs them - the skill loads out of the working tree, so a clone that lacks them
# is still a complete plugin. Both rules are anchored: they name these two folders at the root,
# not every directory that happens to share a name.
/griddle/
/.agents/

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Throwaway harnesses written to prove one thing about the working tree: a fidelity comparison
# against the committed state, a breakage battery against a new test. Each speaks about the tree as
# it stood the moment it was written, so they are ignored rather than kept green: the tests that
# earn a living are the ones under tests/ that mean the same thing tomorrow.
.scratch-*/

# editors and operating systems
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
*~

AGENTS.md